Q: How to invoke UI thread in Winform application without a form or control? A: <p>You are quite close to the solution :</p>
<pre><code>SynchronizationContext.Current!.Send(state =&gt; 
{
    //you shnow inside UI thread
    //invoke some commands (eg: callback that access UI)
}, null);
</code></pre>
<p>You might also call <code>Post()</code> for asynchronous message dispatch</p>
<p>This also works without any form. Create a contenxt in the UI related thread :</p>
<pre><code>var context = new WindowsFormsSynchronizationContext();
//...
Application.Run();
</code></pre>
<p>Inside the thread that use <code>SynchronizationContext.Current.Send()</code> or <code>Post()</code></p>
<pre><code>SynchronizationContext.SetSynchronizationContext(context);
</code></pre>

